WEBVTT

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.770
Takafumi

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.800
Oh, you're awake.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.170
How is that hangover?

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.930
Wh-What are you doing here?!

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:21.140
What's with that? Are you trying to say you don't remember anything about last night?

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.810
Take a good look around and
I'm sure you'll figure it out.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:25.980
Good look around?

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.290
My romantic relationships
are none of your business.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.620
Give me some time.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.010
Welcome!

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:00.010
Kirishima-san?

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.770
So even the mighty editor-in-chief
...of Japun comes to this kind of dive...

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.400
So you really don't remember anything at all?

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:14.280
Well, I suppose salarymen do occasionally
have days where they just want to get pissed.

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:16.900
But dragging others into it as well is something of an inconvenience,

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.160
so try being a little more careful next time.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.410
I hardly need you lecturing me about—

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.540
Take your elders' advice without the backtalk.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.160
Got it?

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:40.300
Oh yeah. You were griping last night all about how you had gotten your heart broken by another guy.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:41.680
I was?

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.890
Hey, calm down.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.810
You didn't say his name.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.440
One more thing...

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.980
You'll be working as my servant for a while.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.190
Huh?

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.240
Dragging me into your drinking binge,
making me listen to you bitch about work and some guy,

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.490
then making me pay the tab
...and look after your drunk ass...

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.830
Wouldn't you say that alone
merits some form of repayment?

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:12.580
Besides, I love taking proud guys
like you down a peg or two.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.540
What! Stop screwing around!

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.210
Don't get so full of yourself!

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.800
Guess the wild bear of Sales is all bark and no bite, huh?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.510
You're a long ways from being able to take me down.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.470
Damn you.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:28.600
I'm sure you wouldn't want these embarrassing pictures getting out as well, right?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.230
What pictures?

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.350
You sure are slow.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.820
The ones I took of you last night, of course.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.780
He—Wait!

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:38.530
Hey!

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.120
This is the worst.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.000
Good morning.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.880
Oh, it's you.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.140
Don't make me look at people
I don't want to see first thing in the morning.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.850
I'm sorry.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.140
You're here early for an editor.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.850
Are you just that slow at work?

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.900
That's not it.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.770
I just have to turn in the project
proposal for the next volume,

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.780
so I figured sooner was better.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.660
You know, it's not like you have to be
so hopped-up about a job you don't even like.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:25.700
Um, you see...

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:29.040
I really do feel that I'd like to try
my hand as a manga editor!

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.830
I know I still have a lot to learn,

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:36.960
so I'd appreciate it if you
could help teach me as well.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.550
Even though, to be honest,
I don't really get along well with you.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.300
Takano-san says you really know
your way around the business.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.430
Of course I do!

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:53.230
But it's way too early for someone like you to be begging tips off of me!

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:59.440
Well, though I don't want to,
I will admit: You do your job well.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.820
That proposal was well done.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:06.660
You can move ahead with it.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:08.910
However...

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.750
If you can't pull it off,
then it's worthless.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:17.670
I'm doubtful as to whether or not
you'll actually be able to do so, but I'll cooperate.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.340
It's my job, after all.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.000
Ah, right!

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.090
I look forward to working together!

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:26.430
And one more thing...

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:27.930
Are you...

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:32.220
...in love with Masamune?

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.230
Yes.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.520
However you may feel…

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:46.240
If you hurt him,
I won't hesitate to take him back.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.490
Just keep that in mind.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:57.460
Good morning!

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:58.500
Yeah.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.010
Maybe someone like that suits him more.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.140
I truly do want Masamune to be happy.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.560
Precisely because I know how bad things were before, I want that more than anyone else in the world.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:20.440
I wanted to be the one to make him happy myself,
but I guess it just wasn't meant to be.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.320
What the hell am I doing?

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.620
The sales promotion data from <i>Japun</i> isn't here yet!

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:40.670
Henmi!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.290
Henmi-san's out at the moment.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:06:59.270
Good afternoon.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:03.150
Hey, we still haven't received
the data for the sales promotion.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.320
I'm sorry about that.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.820
I was just about to come down
and deliver it to you myself!

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.200
Th-Thanks...

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:14.330
That reminds me, the design for the new cover of
<i>Za Kan</i> is finished. Check it out, since you're here.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:18.250
Here.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.370
Ah, I guess it's fine?

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.790
Onodera, that check you just
finished, was utter garbage.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.010
Eh, how so?!

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:28.670
Isn't it obvious?

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.970
Yokozawa, we're going out drinking.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.430
Huh? Why?!

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.220
Aren't you a little young
to be going senile?

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.060
Did you already
forgot about this morn—

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:39.600
Oh!

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:42.350
We were supposed to have
that chat about the campaign!

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.360
Exactly. I'm so glad
that you remembered!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.610
Well, shall we get going, then?

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:48.610
Okay, please take care of things.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:02.250
How is it? It's delicious, right?

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.000
Yeah, it is.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:10.010
So, are you having fun,
dragging me to this kind of place?

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.220
I really wanted to see your grumpy face.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.970
You've got a really twisted
personality, you know.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:19.270
I actually get complimented
on my personality rather often.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:23.560
I'm sure your subordinates have a hard time getting work done under a boss like you.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:27.730
There's no way I'd ever do anything cruel to my cute little underlings!

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:31.240
I'm sure they're a lot happier than
those poor souls under you, at least.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:33.110
That's not...

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.660
Your guys are doing good work over there, so let them know it now and then.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:43.410
It makes a world of difference just saying little things like "good work today" and "thank you."

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.040
I know that already.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.590
Yet you still can't say it, right?

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:53.220
Not much longer and the only one who'll be willing
to put up with your tsundere shit will be your lover.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.720
Who're you calling a tsundere?!

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:02.560
Anyway, why are you being so damned persistent, dragging me out like this?

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:07.230
Didn't I tell you?
I like messing with proud guys.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.940
Well if that's your type - our company's full of them, in case you hadn't noticed.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.190
Like...Takano?

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:15.700
Nah, he's no good.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:19.660
He may be proud,
but he's more sensitive than he looks.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:21.330
It feels like he'd go down with one hit.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.670
He probably wouldn't provide much of a challenge if I really went after him.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:32.340
Well, I guess it was that young sensitivity that helped him get <i>Emerald</i> back on track.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.800
But you've got your own
good points yourself,

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.840
so you really don't have
to be so sensitive about him.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.720
I-I'm not sensitive about him...

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:44.520
You're good at your job and easy on the eyes,

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.600
so you ought to have a bit more self-confidence.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.770
Wh-What the hell is that?
You're grossing me out here.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:58.070
Sorry.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:09:59.490
Hello?

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:01.490
Ah, good work.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:04.160
Oh, I took care of that already. Yeah.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.750
Sorry. I need to drop by the office again.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.260
Oh, then I'll head out as well.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.380
Huh? What about the bill?

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.010
I already paid.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:20.970
Huh?

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:24.390
You, young things, ought to pipe down and let your elders treat you.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.060
I'll pay!

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:29.650
I don't want to rack up
any more debts to you!

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.900
Well if you insist, then...

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.080
What the hell are you thinking?
In a place like this...

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.620
So you're saying it would
have been fine somewhere else?

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:48.760
Like hell!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.830
I can't believe you'd
pull a dirty trick like that!

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:54.210
C'mon, you're a grown man.
Stop whining like a little girl.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:57.420
You're not gonna try and tell me that was your first kiss or something, right?

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.300
Well you just looked so innocent,
I thought maybe...

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.720
But if it wasn't, then all the better.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.970
It'd be a shame if I'd stolen
that from you, after all.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.480
Dammit. I'm playing right into his hand.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:11.600
See you, then. Work hard.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:13.730
I almost forgot...

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:16.860
Thanks for the meal!

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.660
Screwing around like that!

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:30.960
It was a mistake going out and getting drunk alone, even if I had just been dumped.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:36.800
If I'd just gone straight home, I could've avoided getting involved with that guy.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:43.890
Takano Masamune...was pretty much my first love.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.600
He had this air about him that
made him difficult to approach,

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.520
and I was the only one
he ever smiled for.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:57.030
As I spent time with him, I gradually started to fall in love with him.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:01.860
Then, one night, Masamune
was in a particularly bad state,

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.950
and on the heels of the drinks we'd been downing, we finally crossed that line.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.950
And despite understanding
how much he regretted it...

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.830
I finally started to recognize
my own feelings for him.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.880
I didn't love him as a best friend...

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:16.630
Yokozawa-san!

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.340
I was in love with him.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.380
We've been waiting!

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:20.590
I never remotely imagined...

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:24.390
I'm sorry to have called you away while you were busy.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:26.390
that that very same love would be put to a stop in such a horrific fashion.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.390
My apologies to you as well.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:32.350
Thanks so much for setting up that <i>Za Kan</i> corner last month.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.060
Because of that, we've had to
commission an emergency reprinting.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.320
That's amazing!

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.940
With the movie coming out soon,
I'm really looking forward to the upcoming events!

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.110
Thank you very much.

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:47.950
The release date for the next volume should be announced in next week's magazine,

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:50.370
so feel free to make another dedicated display.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.460
Oh, absolutely! Definitely!

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:58.290
I'll be sure to let the managing editor know that
<i>Books Marimo</i> is doing their best to help promote the work.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:02.510
Wait a minute, isn't he the managing editor?!

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:07.760
Oh, Yokozawa!

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:11.060
Perfect timing!
Let's grab some dinner!

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:13.140
Huh?! Why the hell would I—

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:14.480
Pictures!

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:22.070
Dammit! Why did this
have to happen to me?

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.990
So, without a clue what thrill he could
possibly be getting out of our time together...

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:31.740
I wound up getting dragged out for drinks or dinner by Kirishima almost every day.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:34.710
I was certain he'd
tire of the ruse quickly...

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:37.710
...but I was still at a loss
as to his true intentions.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:51.890
I'm home.

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:55.480
I know, I know...

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.880
Subject: (no title)
From:   Kirishima
Time:    21:05

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.880
I want Thai food tomorrow
night!
Let's go here.
URL
http://gochisou.com/thaitom

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:19.380
Again?

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.840
What on earth is going
through that man's head?

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:39.900
Ah, Yokozawa-san!
It's terrible!

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:41.520
What's going on?

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:45.320
We've been fielding calls all morning with questions about <i>Za Kan</i>.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:50.160
They all want to know if the movie premiere date and the cast information are true!

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:54.290
What? We've only announced
that the movie is in production!

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:59.040
No information about the movie was to be released until the magazine goes on sale!

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.250
Where is the leak?!

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:05.000
Apparently it was written on
a fax we sent to the book stores…

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:09.300
The shop in question didn't
mean to cause offense.

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.760
They just posted a notice
about the movie coming out,

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:17.310
and a reader happened to snap
a picture of it and post it online.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:19.940
Then it just exploded from there, apparently.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:20.810
month

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:20.810
day

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:22.810
This day was...

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:31.530
What should we do?

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:34.330
Sorry! This is all on me.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.200
I'll apologize to
the editing department.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:39.910
K-Kirishima-san...

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.210
A word, if you don't mind?

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:44.630
Of course.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.510
You probably know what
I came to talk to you about, right?

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:54.970
I do. This was all my fault.
I'm really sorry for this.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:59.680
To think that the great Yokozawa Takafumi
would make a stupid mistake like this.

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:05.480
This wouldn't have anything to do with why you went and got pissed out of your skull, would it?

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:13.990
I'll bet none of your people would ever imagine
that you'd let your personal affairs affect your work.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:23.750
Because of my stupid mistake...
a year of hard work was just ruined.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:26.880
Come on, don't make that face.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:30.260
I just wanted to have
a little fun with you.

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:33.760
I'm telling you
I'm not really all that angry.

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:36.180
As long as you feel bad for it,
I suppose that is enough.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.220
Wait... How can that be enough?!

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:41.270
We can't exactly take back
what happened, you know!

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.140
Well then...

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:46.440
Why not just play it up
as a publicity stunt?

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:48.020
Publicity stunt?

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:52.650
Just say you leaked
a little info to get people excited.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:54.780
Everything should
work out nicely then, right?

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:57.450
I'm having my people tell
whoever calls here,

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:01.160
that the full details will be available in the magazine when it goes on sale.

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:05.210
Thankfully, none of the really big points got out.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:10.170
So for now, I'll have the author and
the anime producer accept things as they are.

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:14.680
Is it possible that
you are covering for me?

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.890
What else does it look like?

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:18.430
Be grateful!

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.770
Guess that is another one you owe me.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:25.690
It was my fault.
I really feel terrible about this.

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:27.190
Try being cuter for a start.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:28.940
Huh?

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:32.940
It's "I do apologize."
Go on, try it out.

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:34.450
The hell I will!

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.120
Stop laughing!

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:39.700
There you go.
That's more like it!

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:43.960
Everyone around you falls apart
when the wild bear acts all depressed.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:44.910
Huh?

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:48.840
Was he... trying to cheer me up?

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:53.460
Anyways, for now, tell the other guys
down in Sales that I ripped you a new one.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:58.720
You can pay me back by selling twice as many new and back issues of my series as usual.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.850
I'd sell more than that
even without you asking!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.850
That is the spirit!

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:07.150
Oh right, come grab a bite
to eat with me after work today.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:11.980
And make sure you're ready
to go by six no matter what.

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.780
Uh... I've got no choice.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:18.740
I can't exactly refuse him today.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:27.420
So? Just where are we off to today?

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:29.130
You'll find out when we get there.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:33.300
Today I'm gonna treat you to the best food
in the entire world, so look forward to it.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:34.670
Okay...

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.430
Is this your place?

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:46.520
Yup!

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:51.650
It's not very tidy, but there is at least
enough space to have dinner, so don't worry.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:55.070
Hiyo! I'm home!

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:56.650
Welcome home!

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:59.410
Oh, do we have a guest, Dad?

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:00.370
"Dad"?!

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.950
Is there a problem with my being a "dad"?

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:06.540
No! That is not what I meant.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.670
This is my daughter Hiyori.
She's ten years old.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:15.210
And this man here is Yokozawa.
He works in the Sales Department of my office.

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:20.720
Despite outward appearances, he's still in his twenties, so don't go around calling him uncle or anything?

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:24.100
Got it! Can I call you "Yokozawa-oniichan"?

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:26.350
Sure...

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:31.860
It's a pleasure to meet you. I'm Kirishima Hiyori!
Thank you for always taking care of dad!

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:35.980
The pleasure is all mine. Please treat me well tonight. I'm Yokozawa Takafumi.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:39.820
Oh right, Yokozawa?
Don't you have a present for Hiyori?

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:42.990
Huh? Oh! Here you go.

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:48.250
Green tea-flavored
Bavarian cream puffs! I love these!

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:50.120
Thank you so much!

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:51.880
You're welcome.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.420
Let's have these for dessert later!

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:00.010
My Hiyori's pretty cute, right?

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.840
Geez, Dad!
Stop sounding like a doting parent!

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.140
Yes, ma'am.

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:07.810
Come on, get in here.

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:09.560
Oh right.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:16.650
I'll admit she's so cute
I never would've pegged her as your kid.

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:20.150
She takes after her mother.
I'm never letting her get married.

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:22.780
That reminds me, where's your wife?
Out shopping or something?

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:27.120
Wait, you didn't know?
I don't have a wife.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:27.740
Huh?

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:32.250
Illness took her, before Hiyori
was old enough to even remember.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:37.550
I'm sorry, that was really
insensitive of me to ask.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:39.340
Don't sweat it.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:40.720
It happened a long time ago.

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:44.930
Besides, do you really think I'd have cheated on my wife if I'd had one?

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:48.720
You're sending mixed messages
with that ring still on your finger!

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:51.230
What, are you jealous?

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:53.060
Heh, you wish.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:57.110
I just wear it to keep authors
from asking stupid questions.

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:00.070
If you want me to take it off,
all you have to do is ask.

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:02.320
I never suggested that!

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.530
So what do you usually do with her?

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:11.750
My parents live nearby, so if I have to work late, she stays with them.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.080
Why not live with them?

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:18.960
Dad, Yokozawa-oniichan,
dinner's ready!

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:22.170
The distance I'm keeping from them
right now is just right, as I see it.

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:25.890
Thanks for the food.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:30.220
Yokozawa-oniichan, would
you like a beer or oolong tea?

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:34.690
Have a beer. You've got the day off tomorrow.
If you drink too much, you can just spend the night.

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:37.400
I'll pass, thanks.
Could I get some oolong tea?

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:40.110
Eh, you should spend the night...

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.490
I've got a cat waiting for me.

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:45.610
You've got a kitty?!
What's its name?

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:47.030
Sorata.

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:50.830
He wasn't really my cat at first,
but well, some things happened.

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:54.000
He's over ten years old now,
though, so he's an old cat.

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:56.000
You like cats?

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:57.790
Yup! I love them!

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.710
You're so lucky...

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:03.260
I want to get one too,
but Dad said no...

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:05.470
Hey, I never said
you couldn't have one.

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:08.260
I said I didn't mind as long as you think
you could take care of it properly on your own.

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:11.890
I've got a hard enough time
taking care of myself, after all.

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:14.270
Would you like to come over
and see him sometime?

00:22:14.810 --> 00:22:15.560
Can I?

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:19.730
I've been too busy lately with work
to really play with him much.

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:20.770
I'm sure he'd love it.

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:26.910
Dad, can I go see the kitty
at Yokozawa-oniichan's house?

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:30.660
Who knows? I suppose that'll depend on your grades from third semester.

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:33.620
Eh? Okay, I'll do my best.

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:36.210
Ah, I forgot to set out the salad!

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:40.840
I never expected you
to be so good with kids.

00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:43.460
Don't tell me...
animals like you too, huh?

00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:46.930
That's because animals and kids
see people for who they are on the inside.

00:22:46.930 --> 00:22:51.050
You do realize you're pretty much admitting
that you're scary at first glance, right?

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:53.680
Shut up...

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:06.650
Ever since that first night...

00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:09.200
I've been going over
to his place almost every day.

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:12.030
You're still not done yet?

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:17.080
One of the authors broke her deadline
really seriously, and the proof still isn't done.

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:20.040
Then I'll pass today.

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:22.590
Take Hiyori's treat
home with you for me.

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:24.550
Do you have other
plans or something?

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:28.550
No, but I can't exactly go over to your
place when you're not there, can I?

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:31.840
If you don't have anything else to do,
it'd actually really help if you could go.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:35.850
My parents are off on a trip with
the neighborhood association right now,

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:38.480
so she's home alone tonight.

00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:43.730
Eh? What the hell are you thinking,
leaving a 10-year-old girl alone at home?

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:46.900
I thought I'd be done sooner!

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:48.610
I've already let her know I'll be late.

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:50.150
Whatever, give me the key!

00:23:57.620 --> 00:23:59.500
Welcome, Onii-chan!

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:04.710
Onii-chan, did you run
all the way here?

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:07.510
Ah! Did you need to use
the bathroom or something?

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:11.760
I hurried because I heard
you were here all alone.

00:24:12.340 --> 00:24:15.680
Dad said you'd be coming
home ahead of him...

00:24:16.060 --> 00:24:18.270
But I'm totally fine on my own!

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:19.350
I see...

00:24:19.850 --> 00:24:21.190
Well, that's good, then.

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:23.770
Oh! Here, a treat.

00:24:26.360 --> 00:24:28.150
These are adorable!

00:24:28.940 --> 00:24:29.900
Thank you!

00:24:33.410 --> 00:24:34.990
What're you making for dinner?

00:24:35.990 --> 00:24:37.120
Would you like some help?

00:24:37.620 --> 00:24:41.330
Really? Let's see, wait just a minute!

00:24:43.210 --> 00:24:44.670
Here, you can wear this!

00:24:45.130 --> 00:24:47.090
It's better to wear an apron, right?

00:24:47.460 --> 00:24:48.420
Oh, thank y—

00:24:50.300 --> 00:24:55.010
Dad bought it for me for my birthday, but it's too big for me to use just yet.

00:24:55.600 --> 00:24:59.270
It would be a waste to get
your present dirty, though, right?

00:24:59.470 --> 00:25:03.060
You wear an apron so
you won't get your clothes dirty.

00:25:03.390 --> 00:25:05.360
It'd be more of a waste not to use it!

00:25:13.610 --> 00:25:15.950
You really saved me today, thanks.

00:25:16.450 --> 00:25:16.990
Sure.

00:25:19.120 --> 00:25:20.660
So did she say anything?

00:25:21.040 --> 00:25:21.540
Hm?

00:25:21.830 --> 00:25:24.420
Like that she didn't like being
left alone, or felt lonely?

00:25:24.420 --> 00:25:27.340
I just thought maybe she'd have
told you if she felt that way.

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:30.550
She definitely never
mentioned being lonely.

00:25:30.880 --> 00:25:33.050
She was perfectly fine on her own.

00:25:33.970 --> 00:25:34.800
I see...

00:25:35.720 --> 00:25:37.300
So you worry about
that kind of thing, then?

00:25:37.760 --> 00:25:39.100
Of course!

00:25:39.970 --> 00:25:43.230
It would be fine if I just had a job
where I could get home earlier,

00:25:43.850 --> 00:25:48.980
but even if I changed jobs, there is
nothing else I can do but be an editor.

00:25:49.230 --> 00:25:51.360
You're working hard enough as is!

00:25:52.150 --> 00:25:54.490
Kids understand that
even without you saying it!

00:25:55.320 --> 00:25:57.120
Just give her attention whenever you can,

00:25:57.120 --> 00:25:59.870
and let her know if something is
bothering you, that's all you need to do!

00:26:01.700 --> 00:26:04.250
That's a surprise. I never expected
to be comforted by you.

00:26:05.370 --> 00:26:08.250
I didn't say it for your sake.

00:26:09.670 --> 00:26:12.010
All right, I'm gonna head on home.

00:26:14.260 --> 00:26:15.220
Yokozawa.

00:26:16.970 --> 00:26:19.510
I'm sorry. You seriously helped me out today.

00:26:20.510 --> 00:26:24.180
Like I said... I did it for Hiyo, not you.

00:26:24.520 --> 00:26:25.640
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:26:26.140 --> 00:26:27.310
Yeah, I know.

00:26:28.230 --> 00:26:29.060
But still...

00:26:30.360 --> 00:26:31.270
Thank you.

00:26:35.530 --> 00:26:36.280
Good night.

00:26:36.910 --> 00:26:38.410
G-Good night.

00:26:47.710 --> 00:26:48.960
What's going on?

00:26:52.750 --> 00:26:56.760
Man, I just cannot get over that
picture Kirishima-san showed us.

00:26:57.090 --> 00:26:59.430
Yeah, it totally threw me for a loop!

00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:03.640
It was kinda like getting to see
Yokozawa-san's unexpected true self, you know?

00:27:03.970 --> 00:27:04.600
Hey!

00:27:05.680 --> 00:27:08.390
Just what sort of pictures of me
did he show you?

00:27:16.400 --> 00:27:17.320
Morning.

00:27:17.570 --> 00:27:19.320
What the hell were you thinking?

00:27:19.660 --> 00:27:21.910
You sure are energetic this morning.

00:27:21.910 --> 00:27:25.200
I can't believe you're showing other people's
pictures without their permission, you bastard!

00:27:26.080 --> 00:27:28.160
Huh? Oh that...

00:27:28.870 --> 00:27:31.630
Well Hiyo went out of her way
to text me the picture yesterday, after all.

00:27:32.460 --> 00:27:36.340
Going on about how I should work hard because she and
Yokozawa-oniichan were making meat-potato for dinner.

00:27:37.550 --> 00:27:39.590
Look, I even made it my wallpaper.

00:27:41.140 --> 00:27:43.140
Cut it out!
What kind of sick joke is this?!

00:27:43.510 --> 00:27:45.470
What's wrong?
You look adorable...

00:27:46.100 --> 00:27:48.730
Whatever, just get rid
of that picture. Immediately!

00:27:49.020 --> 00:27:51.480
Eh, what a waste...

00:27:51.730 --> 00:27:52.980
No whining, just do it!

00:27:53.820 --> 00:27:54.400
There.

00:27:55.650 --> 00:27:56.610
What a waste...

00:27:57.150 --> 00:27:59.610
Don't get too full of yourselves!

00:28:04.580 --> 00:28:07.870
Good grief, what a waste of time
first thing in the morning.

00:28:09.120 --> 00:28:10.040
Good morning!

00:28:10.710 --> 00:28:11.370
Morning.

00:28:12.130 --> 00:28:15.000
The new volumes of <i>Za Kan</i>
seems to be performing quite well!

00:28:15.250 --> 00:28:17.760
And the magazine seems to be
selling off even faster than usual!

00:28:18.130 --> 00:28:20.340
Kirishima-san's tactic really saved us!

00:28:20.590 --> 00:28:24.300
Yeah, though I'm not sure if it was just
a happy accident or if he was actually that clever.

00:28:24.550 --> 00:28:28.850
It's really amazing the way he can turn
any situation into a golden opportunity!

00:28:30.140 --> 00:28:31.060
You got that right.

00:28:32.520 --> 00:28:36.360
Before, I'd always thought of him as a crafty bastard
who was merciless when it came to his work...

00:28:37.320 --> 00:28:42.400
But he's also a father who can't help doting on his daughter
and who gives in to his emotions all too easily at times.

00:28:42.740 --> 00:28:43.860
That reminds me, Yokozawa-san,

00:28:44.620 --> 00:28:48.450
you've kind of changed since you started going out for drinks with Kirishima-san.

00:28:49.250 --> 00:28:51.120
You're kind of... in a better mood, I guess?

00:28:52.040 --> 00:28:55.380
After all, the furrow between
your brows has gotten shallower!

00:28:56.460 --> 00:29:02.010
The tension in your shoulders seems
to relax when you're talking with him.

00:29:02.840 --> 00:29:05.510
Ah! Is the reason you've been
in such a good mood lately

00:29:05.510 --> 00:29:07.510
because you've been spending
time with Kirishima-san?

00:29:08.600 --> 00:29:10.010
Like hell!

00:29:13.940 --> 00:29:15.900
Sorry. Didn't mean to yell at you.

00:29:16.770 --> 00:29:17.770
It's fine.

00:29:20.240 --> 00:29:22.070
I'm going to go make my rounds.

00:29:31.660 --> 00:29:33.120
I'm exhausted...

00:29:37.920 --> 00:29:40.170
You're coming over
tonight, right?

00:29:37.920 --> 00:29:40.170
Kirishima

00:29:37.920 --> 00:29:40.170
Today too

00:29:42.170 --> 00:29:44.550
Kirishima

00:29:42.170 --> 00:29:44.550
Today too

00:29:42.170 --> 00:29:42.420
Can't make it tonight.

00:29:42.590 --> 00:29:42.670
right.

00:29:42.670 --> 00:29:42.800
Can't make it tonight.

00:29:44.680 --> 00:29:47.010
He has just been dragging me
around as he pleases.

00:29:47.300 --> 00:29:49.560
It's not like I've let my guard
down around him.

00:29:50.430 --> 00:29:54.100
Sure, I might've been a bit touched
by some of the things he did, but still...

00:29:54.770 --> 00:29:59.690
Having Henmi point it out like that and
then blowing up the way I did? I acted like a fool.

00:30:00.440 --> 00:30:03.440
I should keep my distance from
Kirishima-san for the foreseeable future

00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:05.200
and organize my thoughts somehow.

00:30:07.570 --> 00:30:11.330
But what the hell, I just
had my heart broken here!

00:30:12.140 --> 00:30:15.580
So why is he the only
thing on my mind?

00:30:19.130 --> 00:30:20.460
Hey, Sorata!

00:30:21.340 --> 00:30:22.380
Here, dinner.

00:30:24.800 --> 00:30:25.510
Sorata?

00:30:26.010 --> 00:30:28.340
What's wrong?
Not hungry?

00:30:29.140 --> 00:30:31.600
Hey! What's wrong?
Are you not feeling well?

00:30:35.060 --> 00:30:36.900
I've gotta get him to a vet!

00:30:51.030 --> 00:30:51.870
Onii-chan!

00:30:53.830 --> 00:30:54.750
Hiyo...

00:30:55.210 --> 00:30:56.660
Is everything okay, Yokozawa?

00:30:57.210 --> 00:31:00.250
I'm sorry. You came all this way just for a pet.

00:31:00.250 --> 00:31:01.750
Don't say it like that.

00:31:02.380 --> 00:31:05.260
That cat's like
your family, isn't he?

00:31:06.130 --> 00:31:07.510
Ah, yeah.

00:31:09.180 --> 00:31:11.800
He's not sick, so there's no real
reason to be worried, the vet said.

00:31:12.220 --> 00:31:13.970
Guess I just jumped to conclusions.

00:31:15.430 --> 00:31:17.850
I'm sorry to have troubled
you so late in the evening.

00:31:18.520 --> 00:31:20.270
What the hell are you
acting all dejected about?

00:31:20.860 --> 00:31:23.440
Shouldn't you be happy it wasn't
a serious illness or anything?

00:31:25.860 --> 00:31:27.700
You sure you don't need
to get any medicine for him?

00:31:27.990 --> 00:31:28.570
Yeah.

00:31:29.200 --> 00:31:33.200
But he's not a kitten anymore,
so the vet said to keep an eye on him.

00:31:34.290 --> 00:31:37.710
When he said to keep an eye on him...
Did that mean during the day, too?

00:31:38.120 --> 00:31:41.420
No, seems like the usual
amount of time should be fine.

00:31:42.380 --> 00:31:44.920
I'd love to be with him always,
but that's hardly feasible.

00:31:45.420 --> 00:31:46.840
I'll watch him!

00:31:47.130 --> 00:31:47.550
Huh?

00:31:47.800 --> 00:31:50.930
Sora-chan can just stay
with us until he feels better!

00:31:51.180 --> 00:31:54.600
I'm on spring break right now,
so I can be with him full-time!

00:31:55.220 --> 00:31:56.640
Ah, but...

00:31:57.390 --> 00:32:00.520
Just so we're clear:
It's no trouble at all.

00:32:00.850 --> 00:32:02.980
And while we're at it,
you should stay with us, too.

00:32:03.610 --> 00:32:05.940
What? Why the hell would I?

00:32:06.360 --> 00:32:08.950
I'm worried for the cat, sure,
but I'm worried about you, too.

00:32:09.280 --> 00:32:11.200
You look like crap.

00:32:11.200 --> 00:32:11.950
Cut it out!

00:32:12.570 --> 00:32:13.830
This is an order.

00:32:14.660 --> 00:32:16.330
You know what that means, right?

00:32:18.080 --> 00:32:19.910
Again with the pictures he took?

00:32:20.540 --> 00:32:21.710
There! It's settled!

00:32:22.500 --> 00:32:23.920
You're fine with it, right, Hiyo?

00:32:24.210 --> 00:32:24.750
Yup!

00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:27.590
I'll be sure to take
good care of Sora-chan!

00:32:43.770 --> 00:32:44.360
There, all done.

00:32:45.020 --> 00:32:46.480
Thank you, Onii-chan!

00:32:52.110 --> 00:32:54.030
Here. You take milk in yours, right?

00:32:54.660 --> 00:32:55.240
Thanks.

00:32:59.290 --> 00:33:01.920
Like this... we're kinda like
a couple of newlyweds?

00:33:02.250 --> 00:33:02.710
Huh?

00:33:03.630 --> 00:33:06.250
I'm the dad,
and you're the mom.

00:33:06.960 --> 00:33:08.550
Stop saying weird things like that.

00:33:08.760 --> 00:33:11.420
Come on, it's nothing to blush over.

00:33:11.670 --> 00:33:13.430
I'm not blushing.

00:33:14.050 --> 00:33:16.430
Oh, what're you talking about?

00:33:17.310 --> 00:33:18.600
Well, you see, Yokozawa is—

00:33:18.600 --> 00:33:19.430
Ah, it's nothing!

00:33:20.680 --> 00:33:23.560
Hiyo, you'll be late
if you don't head out.

00:33:24.020 --> 00:33:26.730
Ah, you're right!
I'm off, then!

00:33:28.900 --> 00:33:30.820
You sure being the mom wouldn't suit you?

00:33:31.150 --> 00:33:32.280
Go die.

00:33:34.240 --> 00:33:38.830
I've compiled the stockpile info for the manga print-run
decision meeting early next week, so please check it.

00:33:39.490 --> 00:33:41.580
All right. I'll look it over later.

00:33:47.630 --> 00:33:50.090
Looks like I'll be here for a while.

00:33:52.720 --> 00:33:53.680
You're taking a break?

00:33:54.300 --> 00:33:55.300
Gonna have a smoke.

00:34:04.890 --> 00:34:06.900
He looks exhausted.

00:34:08.230 --> 00:34:11.320
I was always the only one he ever let himself show his weak side around...

00:34:11.940 --> 00:34:14.900
...and I guess that was what
made it hard to give up hope.

00:34:16.870 --> 00:34:18.320
I thought I'd finally thrown in the towel...

00:34:18.830 --> 00:34:19.950
...but I guess I'm hopeless.

00:34:20.990 --> 00:34:23.540
I loved him so much that
I didn't know what to do with myself.

00:34:24.120 --> 00:34:26.330
Satisfied myself with just
being able to be at his side.

00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:28.920
I was the one who asked
him to give me some time,

00:34:29.840 --> 00:34:33.010
but lingering affections like that
never disappear that easily.

00:34:34.130 --> 00:34:37.970
Well, I guess the only
difference between then and now...

00:34:37.970 --> 00:34:39.760
is that I know better than
to get my hopes up.

00:34:42.430 --> 00:34:44.730
Hey, Masamune, are you taking a break, too?

00:34:46.440 --> 00:34:47.440
Yokozawa...

00:34:48.900 --> 00:34:49.810
You doing okay?

00:34:50.480 --> 00:34:52.400
Yeah, more or less.

00:34:53.320 --> 00:34:54.780
Eating properly?

00:34:55.570 --> 00:34:56.530
Of course.

00:34:57.860 --> 00:34:59.240
Is Sorata doing okay?

00:35:00.120 --> 00:35:04.500
Yeah, energetic as ever. He's such a fatass, eating me out of house and home.

00:35:06.250 --> 00:35:08.790
So you sure seem to be
close with Kirishima-san lately.

00:35:09.630 --> 00:35:11.290
We aren't close.

00:35:11.790 --> 00:35:13.170
He's just dragging me around is all.

00:35:13.670 --> 00:35:14.710
Really?

00:35:15.090 --> 00:35:17.260
Why don't you just turn him down
if you don't like it, then?

00:35:17.880 --> 00:35:18.890
It's not—

00:35:18.890 --> 00:35:20.260
I mean, it's not like that...

00:35:22.890 --> 00:35:25.350
I thought a lot about before, on my own,
and realized I was in the wrong.

00:35:26.350 --> 00:35:28.650
Whining and complaining about
everything to you the way I did,

00:35:29.230 --> 00:35:30.770
I think I took advantage of you.

00:35:32.440 --> 00:35:34.400
I realized that was
pretty insensitive of me.

00:35:35.990 --> 00:35:39.490
This guy is worlds away from me, with the way I always try to avoid the topic at hand...

00:35:40.570 --> 00:35:45.040
How long has he been thinking about
how to start this conversation?

00:35:48.290 --> 00:35:49.330
I'm sorry.

00:35:51.330 --> 00:35:54.550
I've always loved this
straightforward side of him.

00:35:55.510 --> 00:35:59.470
I was the only one
he ever bared his heart to...

00:36:00.590 --> 00:36:02.100
But what about me?

00:36:02.930 --> 00:36:06.980
I kept my true feelings hidden away within me until the bitter end...

00:36:09.520 --> 00:36:13.940
Seriously! You edit shoujo manga for a living!
Learn to read between the lines a little, will you?

00:36:15.190 --> 00:36:18.440
I'm over it now.
Let's grab a drink again sometime soon.

00:36:19.900 --> 00:36:22.160
Yeah, sure.

00:36:23.700 --> 00:36:28.000
This is the very best I can do,
as a true friend for you,

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:30.710
the person who kept me closer
to his side than anyone else.

00:36:37.130 --> 00:36:38.210
Well, see ya.

00:36:39.920 --> 00:36:40.630
Oh, right.

00:36:41.590 --> 00:36:43.600
Give my regards
to Onodera as well.

00:36:44.890 --> 00:36:46.470
I'll be sure to.

00:36:47.600 --> 00:36:49.430
Even if our love can never be...

00:36:49.980 --> 00:36:52.190
I want to stay his friend, forever.

00:36:53.100 --> 00:36:56.730
I'm sure I'll never find someone
I feel this comfortable around...

00:36:57.440 --> 00:36:59.110
...ever again.

00:37:01.070 --> 00:37:04.370
After all, if things worked out that nicely,
no one would ever have any problems.

00:37:07.870 --> 00:37:09.370
Sneaking off to have a smoke, are we?

00:37:10.410 --> 00:37:11.750
Just shut up.

00:37:12.080 --> 00:37:13.040
You need something?

00:37:13.670 --> 00:37:14.630
Give me a cigarette.

00:37:19.710 --> 00:37:20.300
Got a light?

00:37:22.880 --> 00:37:24.140
This'll do nicely...

00:37:31.890 --> 00:37:32.890
Are you okay?

00:37:33.350 --> 00:37:34.400
What're you talking about?

00:37:35.150 --> 00:37:36.150
Don't play dumb.

00:37:36.520 --> 00:37:38.020
Something happened
with Takano, didn't it?

00:37:39.570 --> 00:37:41.280
It's not polite to spy on people.

00:37:41.740 --> 00:37:45.530
If you didn't want people seeing you,
you shouldn't have made that face in a public place.

00:37:46.370 --> 00:37:48.490
And what does this
have to do with you?

00:37:50.540 --> 00:37:52.790
Sorry, but I'm really
not up for this right now.

00:37:53.870 --> 00:37:55.170
Can I have some time alone?

00:37:55.460 --> 00:37:58.710
If I did that, you'd just dig yourself into
an even deeper hole than you already are.

00:38:00.710 --> 00:38:03.300
Putting that furrow back
between your brows...

00:38:03.760 --> 00:38:06.140
...just when I'd finally gotten rid of it.

00:38:06.680 --> 00:38:08.510
Huh? What are you talking—

00:38:10.390 --> 00:38:11.310
Wait.

00:38:11.980 --> 00:38:16.150
So he figured out who
I'd gotten my heart broken by?

00:38:21.030 --> 00:38:24.240
I never would've pegged
you for such a meddling type.

00:38:24.740 --> 00:38:26.990
I surprised even myself.

00:38:28.120 --> 00:38:30.870
I couldn't just leave you alone, though.

00:38:31.790 --> 00:38:34.500
I did a nice job distracting you
by dragging you all over town, didn't I?

00:38:36.330 --> 00:38:39.590
You're really pure-hearted, though one
wouldn't know it from looking at you.

00:38:40.670 --> 00:38:43.380
You take that first love of yours so seriously,
when nothing ever came of it,

00:38:44.130 --> 00:38:47.090
and then play aloof,
all in an effort to keep from hurting him.

00:38:48.140 --> 00:38:50.220
And what makes you
so sure it was my first love?

00:38:50.600 --> 00:38:53.140
Because you blurted it out
while you were drunk!

00:38:54.640 --> 00:39:00.060
Besides, if it wasn't your first, you wouldn't suck
this much at being in love with someone.

00:39:02.650 --> 00:39:04.650
I'm going to say something,
and you're not going to like it,

00:39:05.280 --> 00:39:08.110
but what you're feeling for Takano?
That's dependency.

00:39:09.990 --> 00:39:11.870
Bending over backwards
to take care of him...

00:39:12.490 --> 00:39:15.660
that was all your way of giving
yourself a reason to exist...

00:39:15.660 --> 00:39:17.620
of putting yourself at ease, wasn't it?

00:39:18.170 --> 00:39:20.380
What the hell do you know?!

00:39:21.290 --> 00:39:24.380
Stop trying tomanipulate people
by acting like you know better than them!

00:39:25.340 --> 00:39:28.010
You sure talk big for someone
who doesn't know a thing about me!

00:39:29.390 --> 00:39:30.430
Yeah, you're right.

00:39:31.470 --> 00:39:34.270
I realize that I don't know
everything about you.

00:39:36.310 --> 00:39:38.940
Why are you making
that kind of face?

00:39:41.020 --> 00:39:42.270
Just get the hell away from me!

00:39:42.860 --> 00:39:45.400
Don't come around me anymore!

00:39:46.190 --> 00:39:48.280
I don't want to see
your face ever again!

00:39:53.870 --> 00:39:54.910
Okay.

00:40:15.850 --> 00:40:18.390
Why did I go and say
that kind of thing?

00:40:18.940 --> 00:40:20.900
I totally took out
my anger on him.

00:40:21.900 --> 00:40:25.650
He is not the type of person
to do something as annoying

00:40:25.650 --> 00:40:27.740
as going around sticking
his nose in other people's love lives.

00:40:29.650 --> 00:40:33.580
So why? Why did he go out of
his way to chastise me like that?

00:40:35.160 --> 00:40:37.080
He did it for my own good?

00:40:39.290 --> 00:40:41.500
He forcefully drag me into his world,

00:40:42.540 --> 00:40:44.710
totally disrupting my rhythm...

00:40:47.050 --> 00:40:50.430
And yet not once...
Did I ever feel that I truly disliked it?

00:40:52.050 --> 00:40:56.010
Even after all this time,
I still have no clue what he's thinking.

00:40:57.970 --> 00:40:58.600
But...

00:41:00.690 --> 00:41:01.440
Dammit!

00:41:11.150 --> 00:41:12.740
It's been two days, huh?

00:41:13.450 --> 00:41:14.910
After treating him like that...

00:41:15.450 --> 00:41:17.290
I probably won't be able
to earn his forgiveness.

00:41:18.580 --> 00:41:21.460
But I can at least offer an apology.

00:41:23.710 --> 00:41:25.750
Ah, Onii-chan!

00:41:26.500 --> 00:41:28.000
Are you headed out somewhere?

00:41:28.300 --> 00:41:31.170
Yup! Going to play
at a friend's place!

00:41:31.630 --> 00:41:33.180
Then here.
Take this with you.

00:41:33.970 --> 00:41:34.970
Yay!

00:41:35.390 --> 00:41:37.060
Thank you, Onii-chan!

00:41:38.350 --> 00:41:38.890
See ya!

00:42:01.790 --> 00:42:03.500
Guess that's your spot now, huh?

00:42:11.170 --> 00:42:12.470
What're you doing here?

00:42:12.840 --> 00:42:15.050
I thought you never
wanted to see me again.

00:42:16.390 --> 00:42:18.010
Sorry about the other day.

00:42:18.640 --> 00:42:20.560
I completely blew up at you.

00:42:21.470 --> 00:42:22.850
I'm actually grateful to you.

00:42:23.480 --> 00:42:27.060
The reason I was able to face him
then without running away was all thanks to you.

00:42:29.070 --> 00:42:33.900
Before meeting you, if I'd bumped into him,
I would've avoided facing him and probably turned tail and run.

00:42:35.950 --> 00:42:39.200
You would've been fine without me.

00:42:39.990 --> 00:42:41.330
Maybe.

00:42:42.000 --> 00:42:47.830
But if you hadn't been there for me,
I'd probably be thinking about him even now.

00:42:48.960 --> 00:42:52.090
So who are you saying you're
thinking of instead right now?

00:42:55.090 --> 00:42:57.720
You don't have to say
if you don't want to.

00:42:58.340 --> 00:42:59.640
...for you...

00:43:02.140 --> 00:43:03.730
What did you say just now?

00:43:04.430 --> 00:43:06.560
I said I was thinking
about you, dammit!

00:43:07.060 --> 00:43:11.570
I've been doing nothing but thinking about you for the past two days! It's annoying as hell!

00:43:12.230 --> 00:43:13.110
About me?

00:43:13.780 --> 00:43:19.370
I kept thinking how you had to be so pissed at me
for saying those things to you. That you hated me now.

00:43:22.580 --> 00:43:24.120
Are you even listening to me?

00:43:24.830 --> 00:43:30.460
Ofcourse, I do! You just surprised me,
so I thought maybe it was a dream.

00:43:30.460 --> 00:43:31.630
Quit messing around!

00:43:32.210 --> 00:43:35.340
Yeah, I don't think I quite caught that.
Could you say it once more?

00:43:35.340 --> 00:43:36.510
Like hell!

00:43:37.760 --> 00:43:40.640
And right after I just finished spilling
my guts here, this jerk goes and...

00:43:42.930 --> 00:43:45.810
Whatever, I've said my piece,
so I'm leaving now.

00:43:46.430 --> 00:43:47.560
Yokozawa.

00:43:48.980 --> 00:43:49.900
Let me go.

00:43:50.310 --> 00:43:51.360
I said I'm leaving.

00:43:51.690 --> 00:43:55.650
You think I'm gonna just let you leave,
after you say something cute like that?

00:43:56.780 --> 00:44:01.660
You know, I've thought this for a long while,
but there must be something wrong with your eyes.

00:44:02.740 --> 00:44:03.910
Who knows?

00:44:04.200 --> 00:44:05.160
Why you...

00:44:05.160 --> 00:44:06.830
"First loves never last."

00:44:08.290 --> 00:44:10.540
Do you still believe that?

00:44:11.670 --> 00:44:13.800
You should just try
falling in love again. The right way.

00:44:14.420 --> 00:44:16.300
If you're in love properly
from the very beginning,

00:44:17.340 --> 00:44:19.550
then isn't that, in a way,
your first true love?

00:44:22.470 --> 00:44:23.300
Besides,

00:44:23.930 --> 00:44:28.060
you've been in love with me
for a while, right?

00:44:29.850 --> 00:44:32.060
Who says that about themselves?

00:44:32.690 --> 00:44:33.900
So choose me.

00:44:33.900 --> 00:44:36.820
If a stubborn asshole like you
is gonna be in love with someone,

00:44:36.820 --> 00:44:38.780
I'm way better suited
for you than anyone else.

00:44:39.240 --> 00:44:41.240
I've got a kid, but I think
that's a plus, personally.

00:44:42.200 --> 00:44:42.910
A plus?

00:44:43.950 --> 00:44:47.200
And I'll accept everything about you.

00:44:47.910 --> 00:44:50.250
You don't have to forget
how you loved him.

00:44:50.620 --> 00:44:52.460
Those are precious feelings,
so hold onto them.

00:44:53.040 --> 00:44:53.840
Huh?

00:44:57.260 --> 00:44:59.840
I said that I would
accept you unconditionally.

00:45:00.300 --> 00:45:02.890
You don't have to change one bit.

00:45:03.720 --> 00:45:05.390
Just so you know,
I come with a lot of baggage.

00:45:06.060 --> 00:45:07.350
Yeah, I know.

00:45:08.060 --> 00:45:10.600
I'm moody, and I aggravate people.

00:45:10.980 --> 00:45:13.060
I said it's fine!

00:45:13.650 --> 00:45:16.440
It's the pain-in-the-ass part I fell in love with.

00:45:16.440 --> 00:45:17.570
Nothing we can do about it.

00:45:18.150 --> 00:45:20.820
And you're fine with the fact that I'm petty and get jealous easily?

00:45:21.570 --> 00:45:25.580
If you're confident that you're loved,
then there's no reason for you to feel that way.

00:45:26.030 --> 00:45:28.200
And I'm perfectly fine
with you being jealous.

00:45:28.620 --> 00:45:30.870
It's proof of how much you care.

00:45:31.830 --> 00:45:35.000
I won't forgive you
if you toss me aside, you know.

00:45:36.290 --> 00:45:37.250
Roger that.

00:49:26.550 --> 00:49:34.910
and embrace the other side of warmth.

00:50:10.520 --> 00:50:15.320
Hey, whatever happened to that "embarrassing photo" of me you mentioned before?

00:50:16.150 --> 00:50:17.660
Oh right, that...

00:50:21.160 --> 00:50:21.990
This is...

00:50:36.220 --> 00:50:38.760
To tell the truth,
while I'm not entirely ignorant

00:50:39.050 --> 00:50:40.760
about how things work
on Valentine's Day,

00:50:42.100 --> 00:50:43.140
Oh, come on!

00:50:45.350 --> 00:50:47.350
I'm not sure if I'm supposed
to give him something, too.

00:50:47.350 --> 00:50:49.310
Uh, cut it out!
That's just disgusting!

00:50:52.770 --> 00:50:57.780
Please come home
as soon as possible,
and don't tell Dad!
Hiyori

00:50:52.770 --> 00:50:57.780
<i>Please come home as soon as
possible, and don't tell Dad! Hiyori.</i>

00:51:00.910 --> 00:51:01.790
Well, you see...

00:51:01.790 --> 00:51:05.080
My friend's making
stuff with her mom,

00:51:05.080 --> 00:51:08.330
but I can't ask
my dad to help,

00:51:08.330 --> 00:51:10.300
and it's my first time making
these from scratch!

00:51:10.710 --> 00:51:14.420
So I was wondering if you wouldn't mind
making them with me, Yokozawa-oniichan?

00:51:14.420 --> 00:51:16.970
So that's what this is all about?

00:51:17.470 --> 00:51:18.300
I'm sorry!

00:51:18.680 --> 00:51:19.430
I don't mind.

00:51:19.680 --> 00:51:22.520
Onii-chan, have you ever made
gateau chocolat before?

00:51:22.930 --> 00:51:26.310
No, but I'm sure if we just follow the recipe, we'll be able to pull it off.

00:51:26.640 --> 00:51:27.690
Let's see here...

00:51:28.230 --> 00:51:31.860
"Chop up the chocolate, pour in the oil,
then melt in warm water..."

00:51:33.030 --> 00:51:34.530
You gonna use all of this chocolate?

00:51:34.990 --> 00:51:39.240
No, I just bought extra,
in case I mess up.

00:51:45.960 --> 00:51:47.210
Hiyori's already in bed.

00:51:48.170 --> 00:51:49.540
Oh, crap...

00:51:49.540 --> 00:51:53.250
Homemade chocolate from my daughter
when my body is absolutely exhausted from work.

00:51:53.250 --> 00:51:55.090
I could just weep!

00:51:55.720 --> 00:51:57.220
Well good for you.

00:51:57.930 --> 00:52:00.010
So... Where are my chocolates from you?

00:52:02.180 --> 00:52:03.600
All right, I'm getting out of here.

00:52:03.600 --> 00:52:04.970
Answer the question.

00:52:05.480 --> 00:52:08.190
I'm sure you got plenty of chocolates
from the women at work.

00:52:08.480 --> 00:52:09.900
You can't possible need more.

00:52:11.770 --> 00:52:12.690
Good night.

00:52:13.360 --> 00:52:14.110
What's this?

00:52:14.360 --> 00:52:16.320
Is it possible that you're jealous?

00:52:16.950 --> 00:52:17.990
Who's jealous?!

00:52:17.990 --> 00:52:19.530
Oh, seriously?

00:52:19.530 --> 00:52:21.620
I merrily welcome all
demonstrations of jealousy!

00:52:22.580 --> 00:52:23.620
Uh, shut up.

00:52:23.990 --> 00:52:24.660
Here.

00:52:27.790 --> 00:52:29.870
I made some for myself
while cooking with Hiyori.

00:52:30.380 --> 00:52:32.130
It can't be helped
if you want them so much.

00:52:33.750 --> 00:52:35.000
This is great.

00:52:35.420 --> 00:52:36.130
Thank you.

00:52:38.130 --> 00:52:39.380
That's all, I'm leaving.

00:52:39.880 --> 00:52:40.550
So?

00:52:41.930 --> 00:52:43.510
Where's your confession?

00:52:44.180 --> 00:52:44.890
Huh?

00:52:45.520 --> 00:52:46.810
Don't play dumb!

00:52:47.100 --> 00:52:50.190
Chocolates for the object of your true
affections always come with a confession!

00:52:50.190 --> 00:52:51.350
Come on, spit it out.

00:52:51.770 --> 00:52:53.060
Those were given out of obligation.

00:52:53.360 --> 00:52:54.650
Don't get so full of yourself!

00:52:54.650 --> 00:52:57.030
There you go again,
always so shy...

00:53:07.500 --> 00:53:09.540
Every February 14th

00:53:09.910 --> 00:53:13.670
has somehow become a day
when I make chocolates for Yoshino.

00:53:14.500 --> 00:53:17.510
I really have no idea
what's gotten into me.

00:53:18.210 --> 00:53:22.890
Tori, your chocolates are so good, so amazing,
so friggin tasty please make more.

00:53:23.220 --> 00:53:24.300
This can't go on...

00:53:25.810 --> 00:53:27.100
And yet here I am.

00:53:27.560 --> 00:53:29.480
I was swamped with work this year,

00:53:29.480 --> 00:53:31.140
so I didn't have any time
to make him chocolates.

00:53:32.560 --> 00:53:33.520
Though admittedly...

00:53:34.190 --> 00:53:37.570
it wouldn't kill him to make me
chocolates one year. Just saying.

00:53:39.940 --> 00:53:41.700
But then again, that's a tall order.

00:53:44.780 --> 00:53:48.080
Yoshino! I've brought the chocolates
your readers mailed to the office.

00:53:48.490 --> 00:53:49.080
Geh!

00:53:53.750 --> 00:53:56.130
What is that sickeningly sweet stench?

00:53:56.130 --> 00:53:57.250
The whole place reeks!

00:53:57.550 --> 00:54:00.260
Why'd you have to come
here early today of all days?

00:54:01.340 --> 00:54:03.090
Were you making
chocolates by chance?

00:54:03.380 --> 00:54:04.510
N-No, no way!

00:54:04.510 --> 00:54:06.350
No matter how you look at it,
this is a chocolate.

00:54:06.930 --> 00:54:08.310
W-Well, you know!

00:54:08.640 --> 00:54:10.390
I was planning on using it
in my next manga,

00:54:10.390 --> 00:54:13.940
so I just thought it might be
a good idea to understand the steps myself!

00:54:14.190 --> 00:54:15.730
Your next one?

00:54:15.730 --> 00:54:17.570
You do realize that today
is February 14th, right?

00:54:17.570 --> 00:54:19.360
It's far too late to be
writing something now.

00:54:19.820 --> 00:54:21.360
W-Well, you see...

00:54:21.360 --> 00:54:22.990
I meant for next year!

00:54:23.240 --> 00:54:25.410
You'll probably have long
since forgotten the steps by then.

00:54:25.740 --> 00:54:26.870
Oh, dammit!

00:54:27.120 --> 00:54:29.120
You're right! I'm lying
through my teeth!

00:54:29.580 --> 00:54:31.370
I was making it for you!

00:54:33.210 --> 00:54:35.380
J-Just... I mean...

00:54:36.420 --> 00:54:38.750
You always make
chocolate for me every year.

00:54:39.590 --> 00:54:42.010
so I thought that this year, I'd do it.

00:54:44.930 --> 00:54:46.050
What?

00:54:46.050 --> 00:54:47.800
O-Oh, no. Sorry.

00:54:48.140 --> 00:54:52.060
I just never expected you
to do that sort of thing for me.

00:54:52.520 --> 00:54:53.890
What's that supposed to mean?

00:54:54.310 --> 00:54:59.020
I'll have you know I think about how
I'd like to do things for you all the time!

00:55:00.940 --> 00:55:02.150
This...

00:55:02.780 --> 00:55:04.110
must be a dream?!

00:55:05.360 --> 00:55:06.200
So, this...

00:55:07.030 --> 00:55:07.950
is chocolate?

00:55:08.660 --> 00:55:09.450
Yeah!

00:55:09.780 --> 00:55:10.660
Probably.

00:55:11.950 --> 00:55:12.830
Still...

00:55:14.960 --> 00:55:18.670
Just thinking about how the ever-clumsy Yoshino made these for me...

00:55:19.090 --> 00:55:21.800
B-But I stand by the taste!

00:55:22.460 --> 00:55:23.970
I gave some to Yuu, too,

00:55:23.970 --> 00:55:27.800
and he assured me
they tasted perfectly chocolatey!

00:55:30.720 --> 00:55:31.640
Tori?

00:55:31.640 --> 00:55:32.970
What's wrong?

00:55:33.430 --> 00:55:36.520
Ah, wait, the ones for Yuu were
for friendship and nothing else!

00:55:36.520 --> 00:55:38.190
I even gave you twice as much!

00:55:38.650 --> 00:55:42.070
Besides, you know that
Yuu doesn't really like sweets.

00:55:42.070 --> 00:55:43.690
That's not the issue.

00:55:45.070 --> 00:55:46.490
Eh? Wait a moment!

00:55:46.490 --> 00:55:48.620
Why are you going right for the bed. Hey!

00:55:48.620 --> 00:55:49.910
Tori!

00:55:50.200 --> 00:55:54.870
And so, realizing that things were the way they were,
Hatori resolved to increase the severity of his discipline.

00:56:02.340 --> 00:56:03.710
It's February 14th.

00:56:04.300 --> 00:56:07.090
Sales at Books Marimo are soaring today

00:56:08.050 --> 00:56:09.800
as everyone wants
to meet the Prince.

00:56:12.810 --> 00:56:15.270
Wh-What's with this huge line?

00:56:16.390 --> 00:56:18.980
Are they all here just
to give him chocolate?

00:56:19.810 --> 00:56:21.940
Uh, I'll just wait outside.

00:56:23.360 --> 00:56:25.990
Yukina texted me saying he wanted
to walk home together, so here I am, but...

00:56:31.280 --> 00:56:33.200
I've got an early-morning meeting tomorrow,

00:56:33.490 --> 00:56:35.330
and he's got classes first thing in the morning.

00:56:35.660 --> 00:56:37.750
So we can't spend the night with each other.

00:56:39.330 --> 00:56:42.420
Though, well, I don't really mind
staying up late, personally, but Yukina...

00:56:44.960 --> 00:56:48.220
I wonder if I should've gotten him
some chocolates or something.

00:56:48.220 --> 00:56:51.760
Hell, no! There's no way a guy
would give another guy chocolates.

00:56:52.100 --> 00:56:57.600
Though I wonder if Yukina's planning on
hauling that huge load of presents home himself.

00:56:59.230 --> 00:57:00.020
Great work today!

00:57:00.020 --> 00:57:00.730
Ah, Yuki—

00:57:00.730 --> 00:57:01.770
Yukina-san!

00:57:02.310 --> 00:57:05.480
Oh, yay! We were pretty sure
you would come out this way!

00:57:05.940 --> 00:57:08.570
Um... These are some chocolates.

00:57:08.570 --> 00:57:10.410
If it's all right,
I'd love for you to have them.

00:57:11.530 --> 00:57:13.910
What the hell?
These girls look serious!

00:57:14.120 --> 00:57:14.910
Thank you.

00:57:16.620 --> 00:57:17.790
But I'm sorry.

00:57:18.580 --> 00:57:21.790
I'm in a relationship with someone,
so I can't take them.

00:57:28.210 --> 00:57:30.090
Kisa-san! You see...

00:57:30.090 --> 00:57:31.800
I made you some chocolates!

00:57:32.010 --> 00:57:33.720
You made some?!

00:57:33.720 --> 00:57:36.430
Yup! Made them myself!

00:57:36.430 --> 00:57:39.060
It was my first time trying,
but it was super fun!

00:57:40.020 --> 00:57:42.350
Oh, th-thanks...

00:57:42.350 --> 00:57:45.570
I'm sorry, I didn't
get you anything.

00:57:46.070 --> 00:57:48.360
Please don't worry about that.

00:57:48.360 --> 00:57:49.570
But, just...

00:57:49.740 --> 00:57:52.780
Man, what should we do?
I guess the shops are already closed?

00:57:53.030 --> 00:57:55.950
Do you happen to have anything you want?

00:57:56.450 --> 00:57:57.290
Wait, huh?

00:57:57.290 --> 00:58:00.080
Or maybe I should give you
something on White Day next month?

00:58:01.160 --> 00:58:01.710
Then...

00:58:02.500 --> 00:58:04.710
I'd like a kiss from you!

00:58:04.710 --> 00:58:07.300
Eh?! You're out of your mind!

00:58:07.300 --> 00:58:08.840
Huh? Well then...

00:58:08.840 --> 00:58:10.340
I'd like you to say
that you love me!

00:58:10.340 --> 00:58:12.720
Why do you keep
asking for so hard things?

00:58:13.130 --> 00:58:16.470
Or wait, should I just be able
to rattle that off without a problem?!

00:58:17.510 --> 00:58:20.100
Eh, do you really
thing it's so hard?

00:58:21.140 --> 00:58:22.100
Oh, but...

00:58:23.520 --> 00:58:26.860
I suppose merely being able to see you today has made me happy enough.

00:58:28.610 --> 00:58:30.650
I-I love your face.

00:58:31.030 --> 00:58:33.240
Eh? My face, again?

00:58:33.700 --> 00:58:36.120
Crap! My honest
thoughts came through!

00:58:36.120 --> 00:58:38.740
I suppose just having you
love my face is fine.

00:58:38.740 --> 00:58:40.080
But it just feels...

00:58:41.910 --> 00:58:42.750
Yukina!

00:58:43.250 --> 00:58:44.250
What is it, Kisa-san?

00:58:52.050 --> 00:58:52.840
Thanks...

00:58:53.550 --> 00:58:54.430
for the chocolates.

00:58:56.010 --> 00:58:57.800
A-All right, I'm leaving!

00:58:59.010 --> 00:58:59.890
Kisa-san!

00:58:59.890 --> 00:59:02.140
W-Wait, the people are looking!

00:59:02.980 --> 00:59:03.730
Kisa-san...

00:59:04.190 --> 00:59:06.310
You should definitely
spend the night at my place.

00:59:07.610 --> 00:59:09.270
Ever since meeting this guy...

00:59:09.480 --> 00:59:11.070
I've experienced nothing but firsts.

00:59:11.900 --> 00:59:13.150
And I'm sure in the future...

00:59:13.400 --> 00:59:17.660
Yukina will continue being
my first in all manner of experiences.

00:59:19.280 --> 00:59:20.540
That's how he makes me feel.

00:59:23.290 --> 00:59:23.870
Sure.

00:59:31.630 --> 00:59:35.050
For some reason,
I feel strangely fidgety today.

00:59:37.640 --> 00:59:39.550
It's because Takano-san
said something like that...

00:59:40.600 --> 00:59:41.560
Exactly!

00:59:41.760 --> 00:59:43.270
Eh, is that so?

00:59:43.270 --> 00:59:44.930
Indeed, I really gave it my all!

00:59:45.480 --> 00:59:46.020
What?

00:59:46.730 --> 00:59:48.350
Ah, it's nothing!

00:59:48.350 --> 00:59:50.150
My apologies.
I'm heading to the restroom.

00:59:54.570 --> 00:59:56.490
Are you not gonna
give me any chocolates?

00:59:56.910 --> 00:59:59.570
Huh, why on Earth
would I give you chocolates?

01:00:00.070 --> 01:00:02.200
And why are you following me?

01:00:02.200 --> 01:00:02.790
Huh?

01:00:03.120 --> 01:00:06.080
Do I need to get a permission
from you to take a piss?

01:00:07.000 --> 01:00:08.960
Not at all.
Please feel free.

01:00:09.540 --> 01:00:10.590
I see.

01:00:11.040 --> 01:00:12.000
So as I was saying,

01:00:12.250 --> 01:00:15.260
Valentine's Day is one of
those days where you give gifts, right?

01:00:15.260 --> 01:00:17.590
Like I said, why on Earth
should I have to—

01:00:17.840 --> 01:00:21.760
People too thick to take a hint on matters
like this will never get anywhere in life!

01:00:21.760 --> 01:00:24.180
Are you saying you don't know
how to be considerate, then?

01:00:24.560 --> 01:00:25.850
Pampered little prince?

01:00:27.190 --> 01:00:28.230
He pisses me off.

01:00:31.900 --> 01:00:36.240
Besides, the very notion of me giving chocolates to
Takano-san is ridiculous, no matter how you look at it!

01:00:37.360 --> 01:00:39.240
But... I don't know.

01:00:39.660 --> 01:00:41.870
Maybe it'd be best for me
to give him some?

01:00:42.580 --> 01:00:45.330
Wait, no way! Guys don't
do that with each other!

01:01:03.470 --> 01:01:04.810
Um, all right, you see...

01:01:05.810 --> 01:01:08.890
I realize that I did text you
saying I'd give you some curry,

01:01:09.560 --> 01:01:12.190
but I never told you to force
your way into my home and eat it.

01:01:12.480 --> 01:01:13.520
Pipe down.

01:01:13.520 --> 01:01:15.480
Washing out and returning
the tupperware bowl is annoying.

01:01:15.480 --> 01:01:17.490
Then keep it,
it's just tupperware!

01:01:17.780 --> 01:01:19.490
Geez, what's with
you all of a sudden?

01:01:20.360 --> 01:01:22.700
Though I guess it's nice that
you're learning to cook for yourself.

01:01:24.240 --> 01:01:26.490
I just felt like having
curry today, that's all.

01:01:26.910 --> 01:01:29.580
But who cooks 20 servings' worth
when they live alone?

01:01:29.790 --> 01:01:31.500
I was just going
to freeze the leftovers.

01:01:31.750 --> 01:01:33.460
Frozen curry sucks, though.

01:01:33.750 --> 01:01:35.000
I happen to like it!

01:01:35.460 --> 01:01:36.670
Well, excuse me,

01:01:36.670 --> 01:01:37.760
I suppose you're right!

01:01:38.010 --> 01:01:40.840
I'm sure you received
a lot of chocolate today,

01:01:41.680 --> 01:01:44.890
so you probably didn't need anyone offering
their leftovers with all that food already.

01:01:45.470 --> 01:01:47.520
Except I haven't
received any chocolates.

01:01:49.600 --> 01:01:50.980
What are you talking about?

01:01:51.230 --> 01:01:53.810
You had a whole mountain
of chocolates on your desk.

01:01:54.110 --> 01:01:56.110
Those were all for
the Editing Department.

01:01:56.730 --> 01:01:59.690
The sweet stench was so overpowering,
I haven't even eaten any of those.

01:02:00.200 --> 01:02:03.240
And I've turned away
any gifted to me personally.

01:02:03.990 --> 01:02:05.780
Eh, but why?

01:02:08.290 --> 01:02:10.540
Because I'm only going to accept
chocolates from the one I love.

01:02:12.830 --> 01:02:13.500
What?

01:02:13.500 --> 01:02:15.670
Huh? Oh no, you see...

01:02:16.290 --> 01:02:17.840
Mind if I have a second?

01:02:18.550 --> 01:02:20.670
Huh? I'll do it, please!

01:02:20.920 --> 01:02:22.510
It's fine.
I can get it myself.

01:02:22.840 --> 01:02:24.930
No, please, sit down.

01:02:25.140 --> 01:02:28.680
Huh? Believe me, the filthy state of your
kitchen won't surprise me after all this time.

01:02:28.680 --> 01:02:30.600
No, that's not what I mean...

01:02:30.600 --> 01:02:32.730
Jeez, Takano-san, please don't...

01:02:40.690 --> 01:02:43.360
Did you perhaps slip some
chocolate into the curry?

01:02:45.160 --> 01:02:47.370
I-I just happened
to put some in, that's all.

01:02:47.370 --> 01:02:49.910
I heard somewhere that chocolate
makes a great secret ingredient, so...

01:02:49.910 --> 01:02:51.960
And the chocolate was on sale,
so that's the only reason!

01:02:52.250 --> 01:02:54.870
You wanted to give me
Valentine's chocolates that badly?

01:02:54.870 --> 01:02:57.090
I didn't, what the heck
are you suggesting?

01:02:59.250 --> 01:03:03.470
So I guess that means I've only eaten
chocolates from the person I love today.

01:03:03.630 --> 01:03:07.600
I keep trying to tell you, that wasn't out
of any affection or anything, seriously!

01:03:07.600 --> 01:03:10.100
Oh, you're so damn annoying!

01:03:14.310 --> 01:03:16.650
You always do
things the hard way.

01:03:18.690 --> 01:03:19.770
Idiot.

01:03:21.070 --> 01:03:25.030
In the end I wound up
screwing myself over yet again.

01:03:25.570 --> 01:03:28.410
For now, I'll give you a hand
in getting rid of all this curry,

01:03:28.410 --> 01:03:29.950
so hurry up and
give me my second.

01:03:33.330 --> 01:03:37.000
I'll give you the whole pot,
so please just hurry up and leave.

01:03:38.710 --> 01:03:39.670
Still...

01:03:40.460 --> 01:03:42.920
Seeing that happy expression
on Takano-san's face...

01:03:43.260 --> 01:03:44.340
...made me just the tiniest...

01:03:44.880 --> 01:03:46.180
...tiniest bit...

01:03:46.630 --> 01:03:48.680
...happy as well.
